<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF says plans 6-yr JGB auction on Friday.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF says plans 6-yr JGB auction on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) plans to offer six-year Japanese government bonds (JGBs) through a price-competitive auction on Friday, a MOF official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders said the offer volume is likely to be 500 billion yen. The coupon rate is likely to be set at 1.7 percent.</p>
<p>When the MOF last held a six-year JGB auction on October 29, it offered 500 billion yen worth of 2.0 percent bonds.</p>
</text>
